{"title":"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be a polynomial with integer coefficients that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec2c566436bfca6f74ea5b134227f79285e144a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(17)=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/207930a30a108a40220f0f3b3652c5e0d34dbd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(24)=17.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d154262ea1037809ed3ac135cd35175975b4fabd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)=n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> has two distinct integer solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/defbf06b987965438e5928b96688e48df84cba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a4ecf12066e05720578b74819681fb175bbf64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"11\" /> find the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa2b0a76d3ff55c1a76ab95778995e974524821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1\\cdot n_2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a4452819ade7c745920afa8c4267291303b9a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)=P(x)-x+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />, noting that it has roots at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d83353d672791bf38c4dce6902d8ae0da5ceb87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)-x+7=A(x-17)(x-24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"18\" />. In particular, this means that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6bdb746be0a977b830a12d15139cf093cc56de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)-x-3=A(x-17)(x-24)-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1fdf2b266f8086f127a963b0444ba595413241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=n_1,n_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"11\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/6/686649bf5c3931ecbf4f030edf04f8ed9e3698cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(x-17)(x-24)=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73d7bbc5d7ab5498188dbe63d88f14c21cbaccd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081a43de6bd30196af7593fd529ed7de17c3c560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> are integers. This cannot occur if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27ebdebcc63282a686cd2d882a8a108961cefde4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\le 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de031396f175a8cebafab43a7b6ebb73d7be842f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> because the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eea6865ba29c58494ccf7525e123570c8db3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-17)(x-24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> will either be too large or not be a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/5838ed5b3cc72d400e4e782e6def348bb1b362af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e56fbd39d7ceba5113524e3ed5ccdf7f36c9dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> are the only values that allow <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eea6865ba29c58494ccf7525e123570c8db3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-17)(x-24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> to be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/c/aec29d7f62c9c94f457d59dbfe2036ad0a77a0dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19\\cdot 22=\\boxed{418}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd4884974beb27346cc90be56bda8873986efb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)-(n+3)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfd17dc4d3100462df726e8eb7f9262783429eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> has two distinct solutions so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is at least quadratic. Let us first try this problem out as if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is a quadratic polynomial. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31a470a0cb952bdf3e2842246020dce798cb9ad8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)-(n+3)= an^2+(b-1)n+(c-3)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"364\" height=\"19\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/8/e98a4fd56faefe0b3f69b678a0c0fedd3cd5314c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)=an^2+bn+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are all integers. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64ba256813de19a6f859801a886d8e7f1af9568a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=ax^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are all integers. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36b3bc207828da7c7c0332254ae1810032f82a29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b74eea39da6cc9e3cf647406ff8c96cc24baf7aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$289a+17b+c=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"157\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd8c4c95c4ac5b79ffe802764aaa37519efb9d75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c86906580e49423129faef479fa71c93f71fb18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$576a+24b+c=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"157\" height=\"14\" />. By doing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc037e7ff8d7649c827ac61ccb1657a3d5a57741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(24)-P(17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> we obtain that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/671eab3cf69e2d7d96f567460c48e555e1a68d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$287a+7b=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175de00a849691f21bf2f084815916940a95195d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41a+b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de93868f0fa1acc64a5b55fec121f4e7e82ff06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-41a=b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/f/46fafb31bf4b75e11e2292ce2acf4198c142300b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)=an^2- (41a)n+(c-3)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"277\" height=\"21\" />.  Now we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/005efb6a27fedc1cb78897dad010eb3e9d46f666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=-41a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/0764dbe35023411c5299c8aa577599e308c14234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$289a+17(-41a+1)+c=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee957c90b629fe2c3579300222fe04fcbc9361c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$408a=7+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> which makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2fb8c8ec9e9c056eb4f2fd34cdbbc2846a97270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$408a-10=c-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"140\" height=\"13\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436fee1e694bc1b86b0bcc40cf13d1a4b1d1366a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)=an^2-(41a)n+(408a-10)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"313\" height=\"19\" />. By Vieta's formulas, we know that the sum of the roots(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />) is equal to 41 and the product of the roots(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />) is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a760d1da0be8b265954ea6315e15703f1c4c8928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$408-\\frac{10}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />. Because the roots are integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568e9a06bc9a16838cedf3233cc5d2ba781e1fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> has to be an integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/4/4245c44f53ff076ca65a1bfe90fac93c0c5373cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1,2,5,10,-1,-2,-5,-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"237\" height=\"16\" />. Thus the product of the roots is equal to one of the following: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/653f4eecceb73b618dfbbf1a1e15119b61877c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$398,403,406,407,409,410,413,418$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"274\" height=\"16\" />. Testing every potential product of the roots, we find out that the only product that can have divisors that sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce6f6c0a023c8d3b667ee34b9e6bb962c87106a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{418}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-David Camacho\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfac0e35e772e25cafb84daed4398dd4e8a2790d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n_1) = n_1+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />. Using the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede74f0ddeb6b80a6ed5d7bac07fa046638733c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a - b \\mid P(a) - P(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are distinct integers, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/077036e2afbb8eecedd1434cf93ebcc9e0ae58e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n_1 - 17 \\mid P(n_1) - P(17) = (n_1+3) - 10 = n_1 - 7,\\]\" width=\"395\" height=\"18\" />and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73655f477e0cb79220b6027a77536e1f63f112e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n_1 - 24 \\mid P(n_1) - P(24) = (n_1+3)-17=n_1-14.\\]\" width=\"403\" height=\"18\" />Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50b46a85276a1b44169b825bba0df7e165d407d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1 - 7 = 10 + (n_1-17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a4db5a2ac5e419d3e3f135096c48d544f5ee031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1-14 = 10 + (n_1-24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa109a900c5096bcb771af296b7387bba7ede8d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n_1 - 17 \\mid 10 \\; \\text{and} \\; n_1-24 \\mid 10.\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" />We look for two divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> that differ by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2d60f7fbccf4a3e3b6e6646d534ce2099141844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2, -5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14623246c61dd239b37c1b5f8b0e5f55a70f520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{5, -2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies these conditions. Therefore, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c7481f3000b3b15b954ffde0ebab86aad59fd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1 - 24 = -5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423ce1a41d83c232d7d973dd13c3afee051cfd42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/d/68d3dea992a0fd685e90394a937f121295206f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1 - 24 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7ff35f23efb295849786f1055a8a7bec31ea51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. From this, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b7623d9814cc5ee9623cf3939d392f23288df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1, n_2 = \\boxed{19, 22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"125\" height=\"26\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164d292e7eda222e46ce89ae6bb71cb607de5acd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1\\cdot n_2=\\boxed{418}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ Alcumus (Solution)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Based on the second part of the problem statement, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfd17dc4d3100462df726e8eb7f9262783429eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> is at least a quadratic. So, we can test that out. Plugging in our known values, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4543cfabf8f9d1302a83c28cab643ffa442114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(24)=576a+24b+c=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46d8472dbeb33121278090270b7abf7a1743d328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(17)=289a+17b+c=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b12a71fe556197e07a7cd415708bea1f4c0286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(24)-P(17)=287a+7b=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175de00a849691f21bf2f084815916940a95195d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41a+b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging in the working <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/defbf06b987965438e5928b96688e48df84cba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c5df946080fc6ec1ee0a560a8e8c5e6699113c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> values, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/682a239492ba1405395dd32c56e1eb93b9e9a43b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$an_1^2+bn_1+c=n_1+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec82fe48a95d494af84ea979fb30365f6552482f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$an_2^2+bn_2+c=n_2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" />. Subtracting the two equations gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/97710dfc8ef131f563d76a7fe32d70431087c905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(n_1^2-n_2^2)+b(n_1-n_2)=n_1-n_2 \\implies a(n_1+n_2)+b=1=41a+b \\implies n_1+n_2=41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"699\" height=\"21\" />.  Adding the two previous equations gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d34d1832fbda17c7e96718fa5cf062624f7ae97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47=2c+41b+a(n_1^2+n_2^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"214\" height=\"21\" /> and adding the two equations we were given gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa1aeb4ebd4d50941a4b4e83f870015b86ed9bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27=2c+41b+865a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"16\" />. Subtracting implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff93dd4da7d554a9241b0b5acafd8016238c6e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20=a(n_1^2+n_2^2-865)=a((n_1+n_2)^2-2n_1 \\cdot n_2-865) = a(1681-865-2n_1 \\cdot n_2)=a(816-2n_1 \\cdot n_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"807\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>So, since both parts of the expression have to be integers, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baa273620a0f87eb72d4f4814e95f81af291a510.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$816-2n_1 \\cdot n_2=2,4,10,20,-2,-4,-10,-20 \\implies n_1 \\cdot n_2 = 407,406,403,398,409,410,413,418$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"755\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Plugging in values that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5be6f5ffedc00f15aa284a929c673da608b96d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1+n_2=41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" /> gives us that the only possible solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164d292e7eda222e46ce89ae6bb71cb607de5acd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1\\cdot n_2=\\boxed{418}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ UnearthedCyclone\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II\" title=\"2005 AIME II\">2005 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204131\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.704 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 544/1000000\nP